# B&B optimization example for clique-bounds.
# A clique of six needs a spill with five registers. Every spill is forbidden,
# so the clique bound proves infeasibility without enumerating prefixes.
# Run from the repository root.
# Enabled:  ./build-clang-modules/pbqp --solve=bnb -Werror -O0 --numthreads=1 --timeout=0.7 -fclique-bounds examples/pbqp/individual/bnb-clique-bounds.pbqp
# Baseline: ./build-clang-modules/pbqp --solve=bnb -Werror -O0 --numthreads=1 --timeout=0.7 -fno-clique-bounds examples/pbqp/individual/bnb-clique-bounds.pbqp
# Observed with Clang 21 Release on Intel Core Ultra X7 358H.
# Median elapsed CLI time over five alternating runs, including startup.
# Enabled: 7.8 ms, 5/5 infeasible.
# Baseline: 707.3 ms, 5/5 timeout.

PBQP 2
NODES 18
EDGES 15
MATRICES 1
NODE 0 6 INF 0 0 0 0 0
NODE 1 6 INF 0 0 0 0 0
NODE 2 6 INF 0 0 0 0 0
NODE 3 6 INF 0 0 0 0 0
NODE 4 6 INF 0 0 0 0 0
NODE 5 6 INF 0 0 0 0 0
NODE 6 6 INF 0 0 0 0 0
